       rect (0.408,0.0) [407.184 x 1177.4] rgba=00000000
        rect (0.0,0.0) [407.184 x 112.4] rgba=00000000
         rect (0.0,0.0) [407.184 x 80.0] rgba=FF656701
          hit (10.0,6.5) [143.0 x 19.0] pointer "vector:/missing/developers.slashdot.org/story/25/12/21/0341243/rusts-vision-doc-makes-recommendations-to-help-keep-rust-growing"
          text (10.0,6.5) [143.0 x 19.0] rgba=FFFFFFFF f=17/700 "Rust's 'Vision Doc' Makes "
          hit (10.0,30.5) [215.0 x 19.0] pointer "vector:/missing/developers.slashdot.org/story/25/12/21/0341243/rusts-vision-doc-makes-recommendations-to-help-keep-rust-growing"
          text (10.0,30.5) [215.0 x 19.0] rgba=FFFFFFFF f=17/700 "Recommendations to Help Keep Rust "
          hit (10.0,54.5) [48.0 x 19.0] pointer "vector:/missing/developers.slashdot.org/story/25/12/21/0341243/rusts-vision-doc-makes-recommendations-to-help-keep-rust-growing"
          text (10.0,54.5) [48.0 x 19.0] rgba=FFFFFFFF f=17/700 "Growing"
          rect (58.0,55.5) [14.0 x 14.0] rgba=00000000
           hit (15.0,5.0) [60.0 x 14.0] pointer "vector:/missing/blog.rust-lang.org/2025/12/19/what-do-people-love-about-rust/"
           text (15.0,5.0) [60.0 x 14.0] rgba=FFCCCC93 f=12/400 "(rust-lang.org) "
         rect (0.0,80.0) [407.184 x 32.4] rgba=FFF2F2F2
          text (30.0,8.2) [3.0 x 16.0] rgba=00000000 f=14/400 " "
        rect (0.0,112.4) [407.184 x 1035.0] rgba=00000000
         rect (20.0,20.0) [367.184 x 1015.0] rgba=00000000
          text (0.0,0.0) [136.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "The team authoring the "
          text (136.0,0.0) [116.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "Rust 2025 Vision Doc"
          text (252.0,0.0) [100.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 " interviewed Rust "
          text (0.0,19.0) [334.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "developers to find out what they liked about the language "
          text (334.0,19.0) [10.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "— "
          text (0.0,38.0) [81.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "and have now "
          hit (81.0,38.0) [256.0 x 19.0] pointer "vector:/missing/blog.rust-lang.org/2025/12/19/what-do-people-love-about-rust/"
          text (81.0,38.0) [256.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF666600 f=17/400 "issued three recommendations "to help Rust "
           rect (0.0,15.0) [256.0 x 1.0] rgba=FF666600
          hit (0.0,57.0) [97.0 x 19.0] pointer "vector:/missing/blog.rust-lang.org/2025/12/19/what-do-people-love-about-rust/"
          text (0.0,57.0) [97.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF666600 f=17/400 "continue to scale"
           rect (0.0,15.0) [97.0 x 1.0] rgba=FF666600
          text (97.0,57.0) [199.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 " across domains and usage levels.""
          text (0.0,76.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
          text (0.0,95.0) [347.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "— Enumerate and describe Rust's design goals and integrate "
          text (0.0,114.0) [364.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "them into our processes, helping to ensure they are observed by "
          text (0.0,133.0) [314.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "future language designers and the broader ecosystem."
          text (0.0,152.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
          text (0.0,171.0) [366.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "— Double down on extensibility, introducing the ability for crates "
          text (0.0,190.0) [321.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "to influence the develop experience and the compilation "
          text (0.0,209.0) [48.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "pipeline."
          text (0.0,228.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
          text (0.0,247.0) [347.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "— Help users to navigate the crates.io ecosystem and enable "
          text (0.0,266.0) [99.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "smoother interop"
          text (0.0,285.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
          rect (8.0,312.0) [351.184 x 684.0] rgba=00000000
           text (19.0,0.0) [277.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "The real "empowering magic" of Rust arises from "
           text (19.0,19.0) [303.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "achieving a number of different attributes all at once "
           text (322.0,19.0) [10.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "— "
           text (19.0,38.0) [316.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "reliability, efficiency, low-level control, supportiveness, "
           text (19.0,57.0) [326.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "and so forth. It would be valuable to have a canonical list "
           text (19.0,76.0) [308.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "of those values that we could collectively refer to as a "
           text (19.0,95.0) [332.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "community and that we could use when evaluating RFCs or "
           text (19.0,114.0) [327.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "other proposed designs... We recommend creating an RFC "
           text (19.0,133.0) [320.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "that defines the goals we are shooting for as we work on "
           text (19.0,152.0) [332.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "Rust... One insight from our research is that we don't need "
           text (19.0,171.0) [319.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "to define which values are "most important". We've seen "
           text (19.0,190.0) [318.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "that for Rust to truly work, it must achieveallthe factors "
           text (19.0,209.0) [51.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "at once..."
           text (19.0,228.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
           text (19.0,247.0) [313.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "We recommenddoubling down on extensibilityas a core "
           text (19.0,266.0) [165.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "strategy. Rust's extensibility "
           text (184.0,266.0) [149.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "— traits, macros, operator "
           text (19.0,285.0) [70.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "overloading "
           text (89.0,285.0) [234.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "— has been key to its versatility. But that "
           text (19.0,304.0) [312.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "extensibility is currently concentrated in certain areas: "
           text (19.0,323.0) [323.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "the type system and early-stage proc macros. We should "
           text (19.0,342.0) [264.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "expand it to coversupportive interfaces(better "
           text (19.0,361.0) [312.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "diagnostics and guidance from crates) andcompilation "
           text (19.0,380.0) [314.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "workflow(letting crates integrate at more stages of the "
           text (19.0,399.0) [311.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "build process)... Doubling down on extensibility will not "
           text (19.0,418.0) [315.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "only make current Rust easier to use, it will enable and "
           text (19.0,437.0) [283.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "support Rust's use in new domains. Safety Critical "
           text (19.0,456.0) [313.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "applications in particular require a host of custom lints "
           text (19.0,475.0) [280.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "and tooling to support the associated standards. "
           text (19.0,494.0) [323.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "Compiler extensibility allows Rust to support those niche "
           text (19.0,513.0) [166.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "needs in a more general way."
           text (19.0,532.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
           text (19.0,551.0) [312.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "We recommend finding ways to help users navigate the "
           text (19.0,570.0) [287.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "crates.io ecosystem... [F]inding which crates to use "
           text (19.0,589.0) [328.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "presents a real obstacle when people are getting started. "
           text (19.0,608.0) [331.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "The Rust org maintains a carefully neutral stance, which is "
           text (19.0,627.0) [327.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "good, but also means that people don't have anywhere to "
           text (19.0,646.0) [318.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "go for advice on a good "starter set" crates... Part of the "
           text (19.0,665.0) [301.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "solution is enabling better interop between libraries."
          text (0.0,996.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
        rect (0.0,1167.4) [407.184 x 0.0] rgba=00000000
         rect (0.0,0.0) [0.0 x 0.0] rgba=00000000
         rect (407.184,0.0) [0.0 x 0.0] rgba=00000000
          rect (0.0,0.0) [0.0 x 0.0] rgba=00000000
           rect (0.0,0.0) [0.0 x 0.0] rgba=00000000
       rect (0.408,1177.4) [407.184 x 697.4] rgba=00000000
        rect (0.0,0.0) [407.184 x 88.4] rgba=00000000
         rect (0.0,0.0) [407.184 x 56.0] rgba=FF656701
          hit (10.0,6.5) [230.0 x 19.0] pointer "vector:/missing/yro.slashdot.org/story/25/12/19/2317247/google-sues-serpapi-over-scraping-and-reselling-search-data"
          text (10.0,6.5) [230.0 x 19.0] rgba=FFFFFFFF f=17/700 "Google Sues SerpApi Over Scraping and "
          hit (10.0,30.5) [126.0 x 19.0] pointer "vector:/missing/yro.slashdot.org/story/25/12/19/2317247/google-sues-serpapi-over-scraping-and-reselling-search-data"
          text (10.0,30.5) [126.0 x 19.0] rgba=FFFFFFFF f=17/700 "Reselling Search Data"
          rect (136.0,31.5) [14.0 x 14.0] rgba=00000000
           hit (15.0,5.0) [99.0 x 14.0] pointer "vector:/missing/searchengineland.com/google-sues-serpapi-466541"
           text (15.0,5.0) [99.0 x 14.0] rgba=FFCCCC93 f=12/400 "(searchengineland.com) "
         rect (0.0,56.0) [407.184 x 32.4] rgba=FFF2F2F2
          text (30.0,8.2) [3.0 x 16.0] rgba=00000000 f=14/400 " "
        rect (0.0,88.4) [407.184 x 560.0] rgba=00000000
         rect (20.0,20.0) [367.184 x 540.0] rgba=00000000
          text (0.0,0.0) [364.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "An anonymous reader quotes a report from Search Engine Land: "
          rect (8.0,27.0) [351.184 x 494.0] rgba=00000000
           text (19.0,0.0) [43.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "Google "
           hit (62.0,0.0) [25.0 x 19.0] pointer "vector:/missing/blog.google/technology/safety-security/serpapi-lawsuit/"
           text (62.0,0.0) [25.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF666600 f=17/400 "said"
            rect (0.0,15.0) [25.0 x 1.0] rgba=FF666600
           text (87.0,0.0) [245.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 " today that it is suing SerpApi, accusing the "
           text (19.0,19.0) [67.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "company of "
           hit (86.0,19.0) [233.0 x 19.0] pointer "vector:/missing/searchengineland.com/google-sues-serpapi-466541"
           text (86.0,19.0) [233.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF666600 f=17/400 "bypassing security protections to scrape, "
            rect (0.0,15.0) [233.0 x 1.0] rgba=FF666600
           hit (19.0,38.0) [299.0 x 19.0] pointer "vector:/missing/searchengineland.com/google-sues-serpapi-466541"
           text (19.0,38.0) [299.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF666600 f=17/400 "harvest, and resell copyrighted content from Google "
            rect (0.0,15.0) [299.0 x 1.0] rgba=FF666600
           hit (19.0,57.0) [82.0 x 19.0] pointer "vector:/missing/searchengineland.com/google-sues-serpapi-466541"
           text (19.0,57.0) [82.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF666600 f=17/400 "Search results"
            rect (0.0,15.0) [82.0 x 1.0] rgba=FF666600
           text (101.0,57.0) [221.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 ". The allegations: Google said SerpApi: "
           text (19.0,76.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
           text (19.0,95.0) [323.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "-Circumvented Google's security measures and industry-"
           text (19.0,114.0) [157.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "standard crawling controls."
           text (19.0,133.0) [324.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "-Ignored website directives that specify whether content "
           text (19.0,152.0) [96.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "can be accessed."
           text (19.0,171.0) [302.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "-Used cloaking, rotating bot identities, and large bot "
           text (19.0,190.0) [207.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "networks to scrape content at scale."
           text (19.0,209.0) [310.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "-Took licensed content from Search features, including "
           text (19.0,228.0) [293.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "images and real-time data, and resold it for profit. "
           text (19.0,247.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
           text (19.0,266.0) [306.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "What Google is saying. "Stealthy scrapers like SerpApi "
           text (19.0,285.0) [321.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "override [crawling] directives and give sites no choice at "
           text (19.0,304.0) [318.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "all," Google wrote, calling the alleged scraping "brazen" "
           text (19.0,323.0) [324.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "and "unlawful." Google said SerpApi's activity "increased "
           text (19.0,342.0) [292.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "dramatically over the past year." [...] If Google wins, "
           text (19.0,361.0) [304.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "reliable SERP data could become harder to get, more "
           text (19.0,380.0) [305.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "expensive, or both -- especially for teams that rely on "
           text (19.0,399.0) [299.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "tools powered by services like SerpApi. As AI already "
           text (19.0,418.0) [305.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "reduces clicks and transparency, Google now appears "
           text (19.0,437.0) [327.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "intent on making it even harder for brands to understand "
           text (19.0,456.0) [327.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "how Search works, how they appear in results, and how to "
           text (19.0,475.0) [100.0 x 19.0] rgba=FF363636 f=17/400 "measure success."
          text (0.0,521.0) [3.0 x 19.0] rgba=00000000 f=17/400 " "
